WEBVTT

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:06.790
If we go over the time limit,
they'll close the finish line.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:13.150
D-Does that mean...
we won't be able to finish?!

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:18.700
That's terrible!
There's no time to be lingering around here.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.550
That's true.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.700
Yes.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.880
What'll we do? Is it because I was...

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.220
Don't worry.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.000
We can easily catch up from here.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.710
Relax, we'll pull you to a safe zone.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.810
Huh? "Pull" me?

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.650
Ami, don't worry. Get ready.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.560
We'll switch leads every 30 seconds.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:46.680
Sounds good.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.780
Okay.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.730
Anyway, Ami, just stick close to us in the back.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.450
No matter what, don't fall behind. Okay?

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:56.980
I'm not that fast...

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:00.360
You'll be fine as long as you don't
fall more than one meter behind.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.330
Okay.

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:06.710
Okay!

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.000
All right, let's do this!

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.540
S-So fast!

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:12.540
The sound...

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.550
Normally, I wouldn't be able to go this fast.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.550
Okay!

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.320
How come I can go this fast?

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.820
It's like I'm being sucked forward.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:42.820
Okay!

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.210
I'm not losing speed at all.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.090
Okay~!

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.460
What is this?!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:20.130
Wow! This is amazing!

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.800
Are you okay?

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.090
Yes.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:33.020
I'm surprised I could follow at that speed.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:36.000
That's because we're acting as a windbreak.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.390
A windbreak?

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:40.370
Have you ever heard the term "slipstream"?

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:42.010
I've heard it, but...

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:46.890
It's a phenomenon that occurs
behind a rapidly moving object.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.420
We're applying the principle to bicycles.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.270
Umm...

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.770
Simply put...

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.600
If the one in front becomes a windbreak,

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:00.220
it reduces the wind resistance for those in the back,
so they can ride more comfortably.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.280
I went so fast from just that?

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:07.410
Bicycles are heavily influenced by the wind.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.230
As you just experienced.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.290
Okay, let's go.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.310
Yes!

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:22.680
Slipstream.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.920
So that's what "pull" meant.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.680
Pull me along...

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:39.940
Even if it's impossible alone...

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:43.780
If I'm with everyone, I can go this fast.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.690
If I'm with everyone, I think we can finish!

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.200
Or so I thought...

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:57.600
This uphill climb after all that?!

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.140
I can't see me finishing.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:01.850
We can't pull you uphill.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.050
What should I do?!

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.010
Overcome it with pure grit and spirit!

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.580
But...!

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:13.220
Ueh... and I can hear thunder as well.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.350
Looks like rain.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.730
We have to finish before it starts pouring.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.610
The wind is...

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:23.730
What's with this wind?!

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:26.830
I'm not going forward at all!

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:27.610
Ami!

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.780
Stay right behind me.
It'll be a little easier for you.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.870
Okay, thanks.

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:40.620
It's still hard!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:49.940
It's tough enough going uphill at the very end!

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:53.470
What kind of sick joke is this wind?

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:01.650
Hinako-san, Ami is...!

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.850
Saki, slow down.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:06.030
Okay.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.810
Nine kilometers to the finish.

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:17.190
Time is up in 35 minutes.
We're going at about 10 kilometers per hour.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.200
What'll I do?!

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:23.380
We'll never finish at this pace!

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:29.800
And yet... I can't go any faster.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:33.690
At this rate, we won't be able to finish because of me.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:38.060
What do I do?!

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.680
Ami, are you okay?

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:43.840
Um...

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:45.900
P-Please go on ahead.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.080
I'll follow later.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.700
What are you saying?

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:58.200
If you stay with me,
none of you will make it either.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.790
Then pick up the pace.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:04.980
That's impossible! I'm already at my limit.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.560
You won't know that until you try, right?

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:08.900
But...!

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:11.210
Ami, you're going to participate in a flèche, right?

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:14.720
A flèche is a team event.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:18.970
That's right, Ami.
If you give up now, it's over for the team.

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:23.750
Even if we don't make it in time,
finishing as a team is what's important.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:25.330
Don't you think so?

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:31.110
Let's hang in there. We made it this far.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.630
We're a team.

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:40.080
Let's ride together,
have fun together, and finish together!

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:48.260
Okay, pedal hard with spirit until the very end!

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:51.150
Yes! I'll do my best!

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:09.900
My body is at its limit...

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:13.640
and they said it's fine if we don't make it in time...

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:15.910
But...

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.090
I don't want to give up!

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:22.410
I'm going to finish!

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.590
You're almost there!

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:27.960
Hang in there!

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.040
Keep it up!

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.170
Go! Go!

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:39.460
The five-hour time limit is up... in three minutes!

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:41.300
Where's the finish line?!

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:42.350
Ami!

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:44.180
I see it.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:46.190
That's the finish line!

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.120
The finish line?

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:52.250
Hang in there, Ami!

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:53.140
One more push!

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:54.440
One last spurt!

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.960
Almost there! I'm almost there!

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.210
I made it!

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.140
What's the time?!

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.990
We didn't make it.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:42.430
We didn't make it.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.750
I'm so sorry!

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:56.510
It's all my fault...

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:58.910
we didn't finish...!

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:02.670
What are you saying?
We made it in the nick of time.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:04.800
See?

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:12.400
Okay, it's 5 o'clock.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:16.900
Here are the finishers of the Azumino Autumn Ride!

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:20.530
Huh? But my watch says...

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:23.200
The time is off.

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.910
That sometimes happens with non-GPS units.

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:31.270
So... I made it in time?

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:32.170
Yeah.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:36.420
That means... um...

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.640
You finished 160 kilometers.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:39.780
Congratulations!

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:50.140
I did it!

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:52.390
Whoa!

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:02.660
I... finished 160 kilometers.

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:05.660
I did it with everyone.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:17.170
Well done! Next group, come on up.

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:24.430
All right, the last finishers are
five girls with matching jerseys.

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:26.590
What's the name of your team?

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.430
Huh? Oh...

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:33.560
It's Team Fortuna.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:36.340
How was the Autumn Ride?

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:43.140
Um... This was my first event,
and I wasn't sure if I could finish,

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:46.570
but because everyone encouraged me,
I was able to hang in there.

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:51.130
I could never have done this alone.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:52.950
It's all thanks to my team!

00:12:55.710 --> 00:13:00.260
You have wonderful teammates.
What's your next goal?

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:03.720
I want to cycle to many more places with my friends.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.200
And...

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:06.960
...enter a flèche!

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.220
Yes!

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.610
Okay, I'm taking a photo.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:18.860
Team Fortuna, congratulations on your finish!

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:29.490
Cheers!

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:34.500
There's nothing like a meal after finishing.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.770
Saki, every meal tastes good to you.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:39.880
Not true!

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:42.860
Eating alone after an event...

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:47.510
and eating with the team are totally different.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:49.650
Well, that's true.

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:51.390
This is exceptional.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.220
It all worked out, Ami.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:55.390
We all finished...

00:13:56.740 --> 00:13:59.650
And reserving an inn for the night was the right idea.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:03.010
Didn't expect her to pass out in the middle of a meal.

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:05.320
She took one bite and was out.

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:07.300
Hey!

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:09.030
Watch out!

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:10.740
Safe!

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:13.160
Nice catch, Saki-chan.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.590
Get a pillow and blanket.

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:17.280
Okay.

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:19.770
She fell asleep with her chopsticks and bowl in hand.

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:23.190
Thank goodness she didn't spill it.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:26.300
I don't think she'll wake up.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:28.930
We'll carry her to the room after we eat.

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:33.570
We shouldn't let it go to waste,
so I'll take responsibility and eat Ami-chan's...

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:34.680
I did it!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.080
I finished!

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:45.440
She's crossing the finish even in her dream.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:48.450
She looks so happy.

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:51.310
Good job, Ami.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:12.940
My whole body aches.

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:15.220
Oww...

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:18.720
Okay!

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:26.910
Onee-chan, are you okay?!

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.800
Yeah, I'm okay.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:32.240
You don't look okay at all.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.630
Muscle aches?

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:44.750
Yeah... it aches all over.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:48.500
Emi!

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:50.860
Sorry, sorry! I couldn't resist.

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:54.680
What's that?

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:58.520
This?

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:01.960
Ta-daa!

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:05.770
A certificate of completion
from the Azumino Autumn Ride.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.410
160 kilometers?!

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.530
You really finished it.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:14.120
Just barely though.

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:19.460
I almost gave up so many times along the way.

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:21.290
But everyone helped me.

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:24.190
So I managed to give it my all until the very end.

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:28.410
What is it?

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:32.960
Say...

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:34.530
Will I be able to...

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.490
Hello?

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:41.870
Oh, yeah.

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:44.390
I'll come over now.

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:46.980
Okay, see you later.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:49.910
Going out?

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:52.650
I'm going shopping with friends.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.700
Have fun.

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:56.660
Yeah!

00:16:58.180 --> 00:17:01.790
Okay... I'll do some laundry.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:26.240
Excuse me, I'm passing.

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:37.950
Did Onee-chan...

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.160
ride like that?

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:49.700
My big sister, who's such a klutz that she trips over nothing.

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:53.810
I can't picture it.

00:17:53.810 --> 00:17:54.720
But...

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:57.470
She looked so happy.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.470
Huh? What's...?

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:15.750
Huh?

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:18.040
Emi?

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:22.790
My bicycle has a flat...

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.040
What should I do.

00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:29.310
Should I fix it for you?

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:32.900
Onee-chan... You can fix it?

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:34.140
Probably.

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:36.650
They taught me how.

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:42.670
First, you take this and this off.

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:44.660
And do this...

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:48.660
Then pull out the tube.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:52.290
Onee-chan...

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.460
Huh? What is it?

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:56.920
Aren't bicycles really complicated?

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:59.440
Well, yeah...

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:03.610
It's complicated and I failed so many times.

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:04.910
But...

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:06.180
But?

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:10.970
When you can do something
you couldn't before, it's a great feeling.

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:15.940
And it gives you the confidence
to try things that are hard.

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:21.470
It's hard and complicated,
but that's the fun part.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:27.830
You really did change, Onee-chan.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:32.330
The old you would never have tried something like this!

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:35.560
In fact, you're really proactive now.

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:39.880
You could be right.

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:46.600
Definitely! I still think cycling 160 kilometers is amazing!

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:50.350
Emi, hearing you say that is embarrassing.

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:55.890
Here, try it out.

00:20:55.890 --> 00:20:56.980
Yup.

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:59.050
I think it's okay, but...

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:06.830
How is it? Does anything feel off?

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:09.100
Nope, all good. It's perfect!

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:11.750
All right! I did it!

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:14.370
Onee-chan, you're getting carried away.

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:18.880
Sorry, you'll be late meeting your friends.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:23.380
It's okay. I had them go ahead.
I can catch up to them at the department store.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:26.870
Then you'd better go. Be careful.

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:28.170
Okay. Bye!

00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:33.710
Onee-chan!

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:42.280
Thanks.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.470
You're welcome!

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:33.520
Somehow I managed to complete the Autumn Ride!

00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:36.950
I'll cherish my certificate and photos with everyone forever!

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:40.940
Emi was happy for me too.
I wonder if I'm becoming a more reliable sister.

00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:45.000
Next time on Long Riders:
"The Moment the City Starts to Move."
